A||||13||Black87GT||How do I check if the speed-up light is working etc...||||1||
Z||000000||Black87GT||12-30-2001||07:30 PM||||Hi,  As you have guessed I drive a Black 87 GT 3.1 V6.  I want to know how I can check if a (warning) light next to the speedometer is working.<P>I know my Turning signal lights work, my Brake warning light works, my Hi_beamer light works and my AJAR light works<BR>But how do I know the rest is working? never seen the service soon light (which is good) but how do I know if it will burn if it is supposed to burn.  Is there a way to check if all the lightsare working (or leds or whatever they are called).<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||12-30-2001||07:32 PM||||when you turn your key to run position (just before the crank) the "cluster" goes into a bulb check mode. It is then that you can see if your lights light up, the ones that are controled by the ECM atleast. ie check engine light.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black87GT||12-30-2001||07:36 PM||||With run mode you mean turn the key to start the engine or do you mean turn the key to the posisition just before starting engine?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black87GT||12-30-2001||07:38 PM||||I don think my check engine light is working.<BR>Any other light that should light up if I turn my key?   <P>Just want to check.  Still have warrantee on the car, better check everything now. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||12-31-2001||01:06 AM||||When you turn the key to the on position all of the lights should light. Your check engine light should flash once and stay on along with the alternator guage and oil pressure guage lights. <P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black87GT||12-31-2001||05:58 AM||||My oil pressure and volt meter light stays on.<BR>The brake stays on (of course because it is on the brake).  And that is all I see.  Looks loke some of the importany lights dont work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-31-2001||07:19 AM||||one is an 'upshift' lite if its a stick, supposed to come on when your supposed to shift for best economy. It will come on only when you wind it up in a gear going down the road (vacumm controlled). Its not on an automatic car, even though the space is still there. <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||12-31-2001||08:36 AM||||V6's don't have upshift lights.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||12-31-2001||09:25 AM||||More specifically, the V6 instrument panels have the necessary lens, bulb-mounting hole and dash opening for the Shift lights, but the wiring to activate the bulb is not used in the V6-equipped models. (At least on the '88's.. I don't have direct, hands-on experience with previous years of V6's...)||||reg||1
Z||000009||DrDave||12-31-2001||10:45 AM||||     My 85 GT has the shift lite.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black87GT||12-31-2001||11:25 AM||||I got my hands on a 88 GT manual.  In the manual it mentiones that the speed-upo light should be there.  Not sure about 87, but this proves that also V6 GT have speed-up light.  <P>I will let the dealer check it out. <BR>I want to be sure that the engine check light is working and the rest of the lights is working.<P>Have to go back anyway to install my Leather seats and leather doorpanels.  And change oil etc.<BR>||||reg||12
